	(text "Power: the USB connector of the Pico feeds +5V through JP1 and D2,\nand +5V feeds VSYS through D1, so one cable is enough for small loads.\nCut JP1 to keep the carrier off the USB port of the computer."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 162.56 142.24 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "27c005bc-37be-5b51-b22c-ac19c3053915")
	)
	(text "U1 is a Raspberry Pi Pico 2 on two 1x20 sockets, the only programmable\npart of the instrument. A Pico 2 W fits the same sockets.\nPIO block 0 (GP16, GP17, GP19 to GP21) clocks the converter and reads its data and\nthe side data in the same word. PIO block 1 (GP2 to GP10) is the range\nsequencer: comparators in, gates and multiplexer address out.\nReset or no firmware: every pin is an input pulled low, and the pull-downs\nat the gate drivers and at the regulator enable keep every switch open."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20.32 20.32 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "8fbeda57-b742-5f64-a41a-744c42efd160")
	)
